    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕraequātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		peraequo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a making perfectly equal</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">temporum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">similitudinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 29</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>an equalizing</i>, <i>equal
				distribution</i> of taxes, Cod. Th. 5, 4, 3.</div>
